#!/bin/sh
#
# Secret env vars resolved by chezmoi at apply time and exported by
# every shell. The path in the source tree is
# `dot_config/zsh/private_secrets.sh.tmpl`; chezmoi renders it to
# `~/.config/zsh/secrets.sh` with mode 0600 (the `private_` prefix).
#
# Sourced by `~/.config/zsh/environment.sh`, which is in turn sourced
# by `~/.zshenv` — so the env vars defined here are available to every
# zsh shell AND every subprocess invoked from one (including pi
# extensions, GUI apps launched from the shell, etc.).
#
# To add a secret:
#   1. Store the value in 1Password under
#      `op://Private/<Item>/<field>` (or another vault if appropriate).
#   2. Append a line here (see README.md for syntax — the actual
#      template directives have to live in a `.tmpl` file like this
#      one, not in a comment, or chezmoi would expand them).
#   3. Run `chezmoi apply`.
#   4. Open a new shell or `. ~/.config/zsh/environment.sh` to pick up.
#
# To rotate a secret:
#   Update the value in 1Password, then `chezmoi apply`.
#
# On a fresh machine, `op signin` (once per account) is required before
# `chezmoi apply` can resolve any `op://` references in this file.
#
# sh-compatible: this file is sourced under /bin/sh in some contexts
# (chezmoi's environment.sh chain). Avoid zsh-only syntax.

